{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_review0008", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Two tests fail, both in `parse`:\n\n1. **Bracketed levels** like `[WARN]` keep their brackets, so `bracketed_level` sees `\"[WARN]\"` instead of `\"warn\"`.\n2. **Empty messages** return `None`, because `parts.next()?` bails when a line has no message.\n\nThe fix is small: trim the brackets, lower-case the level, and treat a missing message as empty.\n\n```rust\nlet level = parts.next()?.trim_matches(|c| c == '[' || c == ']');\nlet msg = parts.next().unwrap_or(\"\");\n```\n\nI'll make that change now."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "af9c8cb7-9d7a-4b6b-9753-95decd27b4f6"}
